      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "La vez pasada, Apolo mató a la serpiente Pitón y fundó su oráculo en Delfos.",
          "en": "Last time, Apollo killed the Python and built his oracle at Delphi."
        },
        {
          "es": "Pero lejos de allí, en una cueva oscura del monte Cilene, un nuevo dios estaba a punto de nacer.",
          "en": "But far away, in a dark cave on Mount Cyllene, a new god was about to be born."
        },
        {
          "es": "Allí vivía Maya, una ninfa tímida. Las ninfas son espíritus amables de la naturaleza.",
          "en": "There lived Maia, a shy nymph. Nymphs are gentle spirits of nature."
        },
        {
          "es": "Zeus, el rey de los dioses, la visitaba de noche, mientras su esposa Hera dormía.",
          "en": "Zeus, the king of the gods, visited her at night, while his wife Hera slept."
        },
        {
          "es": "Una mañana, al amanecer, Maya tuvo un hijo. Se llamaba Hermes.",
          "en": "One morning, at dawn, Maia had a baby boy. His name was Hermes."
        },
        {
          "es": "Y en su primer día de vida, este bebé le robaría a Apolo.",
          "en": "And on his very first day of life, this baby would rob Apollo."
        }
